      DECLARATION OF MICHELLE A. PEDROZA IN SUPPORT OF EL PASO
      ELECTRIC COMPANY’S SECOND PROOF OF NOTICE TO CUSTOMERS


I, Michelle A. Pedroza, pursuant to Rule 1-011 NMRA, state as follows:

       1.      I affirm in writing under penalty of perjury under the laws of the State of New

Mexico that the following statements are true and correct.

       2.      I am over 18 years of age and have personal knowledge of the facts stated herein.

       3.      I am employed by El Paso Electric Company (“EPE”) as a Regulatory Project

Manager.     My business address is 100 N. Stanton Street, El Paso, Texas 79901.             My

responsibilities include the preparation of rate and regulatory filings and compliance with the

various regulatory requirements of the jurisdictions in which EPE operates.

       4.      EPE was required by Order Defining Second Notice and Social Media Campaign

issued on September 24, 2026, to proceed to conduct a social media campaign from September

28 through October 12, 2026.

       5.      In compliance with these notification requirements, I hereby certify that EPE ran

social media ads between September 28 – October 12, 2026, targeting New Mexico customer

zip codes, utilizing relevant professional and interest-based targeting criteria, including

government agencies and individuals with interests related to energy and utility services.

Additionally, the advertisement provided a direct link to Advice Notice No. 317, EPE’s

complete Amended Application package, and Second Notice posted on EPE’s website,
                                                1
 facilitating customer access to and review of the notice. A copy of the Proof of Campaign report

is attached hereto as Attachment A.

        6.     The approved Notice, the complete Amended Application package, and Advice

Notice No. 317 were posted on EPE’s website at https://www.epelectric.com/company/public-

notices/application-of-epe-company-for-revision-of-its-retail-electric-rates on September 25,

2026.

        7.     The foregoing Declaration of Michelle A. Pedroza together with all attachments

therein is true and accurate based on my knowledge and belief.

        8.     I submit this Declaration, based upon my personal knowledge and upon

information and belief, in support of EPE’s Application of El Paso Electric Company for

Revision of its Retail Electric Rates Pursuant to Advice Notice No. 317.



        FURTHER, DECLARANT SAYETH NAUGHT.

        I declare under penalty of perjury that the foregoing is true and correct.

        Executed on October 16, 2026.

                                                  __/s/ Michelle A. Pedroza____
                                                      MICHELLE A. PEDROZA




