glossary


    ●   Impressions: The number of times an advertisement was displayed to users

    ●   Reach: The number of unique people who saw the ad at least once.

    ●   Frequency: The average number of times each person saw the ad.

    ●   Link Clicks: The number of times people clicked the ad's link to visit the landing page.

    ●   CTR (Click-Through Rate): The percentage of people who clicked on the ad after seeing it. Higher CTR usually means
        the ad is relevant and grabbing attention.

         ○    The average CTR for Facebook ads is 1.71% across all industries. Source: Sprout Social
